description:
Automation endpoints each build their {ok, error} response by hand. Counted in ixdar.automation (DSL-50 worktree): 89 places set ok=false across 42 files, 70 of them followed by the error message line; 40 places set ok=true; 17 use the bare "ok" / "error" string literals instead of a constant; 40 files declare their own `public static final String OK = "ok"` and 33 their own `ERROR = "error"`; and six endpoints carry a private copy of the same helper (failure in NodeInspect, Holes, Topology, Export, SwitchModel; failed in ring Add):

    private static JsonObject failure(String message) {
        JsonObject error = new JsonObject();
        error.addProperty(OK, false);
        error.addProperty(ERROR, message);
        return error;
    }

Every endpoint already extends ixdar.automation.AutomationEndpoint. Put one OK and one ERROR constant and one failure(String message) on AutomationEndpoint, plus a success() returning a JsonObject with ok=true if the success side turns out to repeat the same shape; make every endpoint use them; delete the six helper copies, the per-endpoint OK/ERROR constants and the hand-built error objects. Response JSON stays byte-for-byte the same (key names and order), so the Python client and automation_routes.json are unaffected. No renames.
